From: mscharged-port
Subject: Copy the DWC server browser command identifier without its NUL
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8
Classification: native libc compatibility

DWCi_SendSBMsgCommand fills the four-byte identifier of its message header
with strcpy(identifier, "SBCM"), which writes five bytes: the terminator
lands in the first byte of version, assigned on the next line, so the
packet was right on the Wii. With _FORTIFY_SOURCE, which macOS enables by
default, the copy becomes __memcpy_chk(identifier, "SBCM", 5, 4) and the
game aborts with "detected buffer overflow" whenever matchmaking sends a
server browser command (any-player matches, and the address of server and
client or distant-friend matches).

Natively only the four characters are copied; the packet is unchanged. The
Korean copy (R4QK01/) copies into the whole header and was not affected.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
index f7554b88..c71ed6f8 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
@@ -2573,7 +2573,15 @@ static SBError DWCi_SendSBMsgCommand(
         len = 0;
     }
 
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+    // The identifier is four characters with no terminator: strcpy wrote
+    // its NUL into version, which is set right after. A fortified libc
+    // (macOS) aborts on that overflow; copy the four characters alone.
+    memcpy(senddata.header.identifier, DWC_SB_COMMAND_STRING,
+        sizeof(senddata.header.identifier));
+#else
     strcpy(senddata.header.identifier, DWC_SB_COMMAND_STRING);
+#endif
     senddata.header.version = DWCi_HtoLEl(DWC_MATCHING_VERSION);
     senddata.header.command = command;
     senddata.header.size = (u8)(sizeof(u32) * len);
